  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/... \nIssued at 1241 PM MDT Wed Aug 5 2026\n\nFriday through Sunday...Upper ridge amplifies over the Four Corners \nfor Fri and Sat, and hot, dry conditions settle in. High temps each \nday are expected to climb into the upper 80s to lower 90s for the \nhigh valleys, and mid 90s to low 100s for the plains. By Sunday the \nhigh pressure begins to flatten out, and the center of the ridge \nshifts slightly to the west. Long range models are trending towards \na gradual increase in moisture for the higher terrain, but the \nplains will remain dry. Given how hot it will be, spotty critical \nfire weather conditions will definitely develop. Currently, wind \ngusts seem to be the limiting factor and will restrict areal \ncoverage.\n\nMonday through Wednesday...Monday still looks to be a very hot day \nregionwide, with afternoon readings similar to the weekend. However, \naround 5 degrees of cooling is then forecast for Tuesday and \nWednesday, likely in response to increasing precipitation chances \nand cloud cover. Shower and thunderstorm chances jump up \nconsiderably for the start of the next work week, mainly over the \nhigher tarrin but also spilling over across the I-25 Corridor. \nUnfortunately, the far eastern plains stay dry at this time. If this \nprecip forecast persists, look for max temp forecasts to start \ncooling even more over the next few days. Moore",
